 that  kind of fits with like the core idea and  conceit of sonic where it's like he is a  action platformer like protagonist yeah  we did face like a mini boss called the  ninja that it was more like oh no this  is kind of like just getting in its face  and like dodging and then like punching  it in the back and i'm like wow this is  a that that didn't really work for me as  well i was not enjoying that as much so  i i do really like the like the ones  that you were talking about the ones  where it's like oh i am platforming and  fighting like at the same time it gave  me very shadow of the colossus hyper  light drifter like those sort of vibes  and i think that works for sonic so my  hope is that we see  more of those uh throughout the game  there was like that boss fight where  it's like oh you had to like circle  around and to like slowly knock down his  head so that you could actually like uh  attack him and finish him off i'm like  that was really cool i did enjoy that  but man that ninja boss fight yes no  honestly the ninja boss fight again  feels very breath of the wild inspired  to me because  um that whole like dodge you gets a  little slow time to hit the enemy a  little bit  is what breath of the wild did so it  feels like again it pulled away from  that i also love that that boss you're  talking about there's one where you use  a special move by circling around it to  stun it that was another one that i  liked because it uses the mechanics but  his name is just tower so i thought that  was kind of funny i'm like oh okay tower  that's  that's the boss all right tower although  i do wonder and we should talk a little  bit about like the story or i guess lack  of story that we really saw with this  this idea that's like oh it's just it's  just ninja it's just tower like we saw  these items that it's like oh if you  collect enough of these you can save amy  it's like save amy like what's happened  to amy and then we had a cut scene where  it's like we saw 